<div class="keyfind"><b>Summary</b><p class="sum">Owners of growing Bangladeshi businesses run many desks, ledgers and sometimes several companies at once. The data sits in an ERP, but getting a straight answer means asking an accountant, waiting for a report or reading screens that were never designed for decisions. EON sits on top of a running ERP as one brain with one memory. You ask by voice or text, in Bangla, English or Banglish. It reads the live data, computes the answer, explains the rule it used and recommends an action. Every morning it briefs; approvals queue in one place; nothing is saved until you say yes.</p><ol class="rail" aria-label="Stage: Validate (3 of 5)"><li class="on"><span>Discover</span></li><li class="on"><span>Develop</span></li><li class="cur"><span>Validate</span></li><li class=""><span>Brief</span></li><li class=""><span>Implement</span></li></ol><p class="sdgline">SDGs <span class="sdgt sdgc-8" title="SDG 8: Decent Work">8</span><span class="sdgt sdgc-9" title="SDG 9: Industry & Innovation">9</span></p></div>
<h2>The problem</h2><p>Owners of growing Bangladeshi businesses run many desks, ledgers and sometimes several companies at once. The data sits in an ERP, but getting a straight answer means asking an accountant, waiting for a report or reading screens that were never designed for decisions.</p><h2>The solution</h2><p>EON sits on top of a running ERP as one brain with one memory. You ask by voice or text, in Bangla, English or Banglish. It reads the live data, computes the answer, explains the rule it used and recommends an action. Every morning it briefs; approvals queue in one place; nothing is saved until you say yes.</p><h2>How it works</h2><ol class="how"><li><b>Understand.</b> Its own intent model understands Bangla, English and Banglish natively, without translating to English first.</li><li><b>Read.</b> It reads the ERP database through read-only access: accounts, payroll, HR and attendance, expenses, CRM, tasks and projects.</li><li><b>Compute.</b> Totals, ageing and ledgers are computed in the database; forecasting and anomaly detection run in a small analytics layer.</li><li><b>Answer and act.</b> It answers with the numbers behind the answer, drafts reminders and notices, and can open screens or fill forms after your confirmation.</li><li><b>Degrade gracefully.</b> If the server or a language model is unavailable, a rule-based brain keeps answering, so the system never goes silent.</li></ol><p>Presented at the AI Business Summit 2026, Dhaka.</p>
